{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788181112,"nonce":"eoPHJ8KXKAFh4xx79HZObLRUa0o=","title":"1.9 Placement must be exact-or-refuse: things slide silently today","message":"Wave 1 — substrate honesty. Depends: none (fix is local). BLOCKS 3.3.\nFiled by the orchestrator, session 6, BORGES, at Evan's call.\n\nThe bug, reproduced live\n\n`dev:spawn-thing` uses `GenPlace.TryPlaceThing(..., ThingPlaceMode.Near)`. When\nthe requested cell is occupied, Near does what it is designed to do: it finds a\nnearby free cell and puts the thing THERE, and returns true. Measured on the\nbench twice in one session:\n\n    dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Bed\", stuff:\"WoodLog\", pos:[112,108]}\n      -\u003e ok:true, placed:1, failed:(absent), spawned[0].at = [113,108]\n\n    dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Steel\", count:75, pos:[100,113]}\n      -\u003e ok:true, placed:75, failed:(absent), spawned[0].at = [101,113]\n\nBoth slid one cell and reported unqualified success. Evan's reaction, and he is\nright: \"things can just slide over? that's no good.\"\n\nWhy it is worse than it looks\n\nThe information is technically present — `data.at` is what was ASKED for and\n`data.spawned[].at` is where it WENT — but nothing compares them, and the two\nfields an agent will actually read (`ok` and `placed`) both say it worked. So\nthe agent's model of the map silently diverges from the map. Every later verb\nthat references the thing by position is then wrong, and nothing ever says so.\n\nNote what already works and must not be broken: OUTRIGHT failure IS reported\nwell. `failed[]` carries the cell, the reason and `Blockers.Describe` of what is\nin the way; the loop breaks rather than continuing; `requested` vs `placed`\nexposes a partial stack; and buildings get a `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` pre-check so\na refusal is a structured error instead of a vanilla `Log.Error` (which would\nbreach the zero-red-errors invariant). This issue is only about the case where\nthe game QUIETLY SUCCEEDS SOMEWHERE ELSE.\n\nScope\n\n- `dev:spawn-thing` (and any other verb reaching `ThingPlaceMode.Near`) compares\n  the requested cell against the actual one and reports the difference. A\n  `displaced` field naming both cells, the distance, and what was in the way —\n  never a bare success.\n- Add an explicit `exact:true` argument that refuses rather than slides, and\n  make it the DEFAULT for anything a caller sited deliberately. `Near` is a\n  convenience for \"drop this pile somewhere around here\", which is a different\n  intent and should be asked for by name.\n- Audit every current `GenPlace`/`GenSpawn` call site in the mod for the same\n  shape. `dev:spawn-pawn` is the obvious second one.\n\nTHE REASON THIS IS P1 AND BLOCKS 3.3\n\n3.3 is `place-layout` — building a house from a baseviz layout IR. If each\nblueprint nudges a cell when its target is blocked, the result is not the house\nthat was asked for: walls stop meeting, doors open into rock, and the agent\nkeeps building against a floor plan that no longer describes the world. A\nlayout verb must be **exact-or-refuse, never nudge**, and it must report per-cell\nfailures in `Blockers.cs`'s taxonomy so the agent can choose between \"clear it\nand retry\" and \"site it elsewhere\" — which is exactly what DESIGN's blocker\ndecision already says, and what a silent slide defeats.\n\n3.3 has not started. This lands first, or 3.3 inherits the defect.\n\nAcceptance\n\n- Spawning onto an occupied cell with the default settings REFUSES, naming the\n  requested cell, the blocker (via `Blockers.Describe`) and its `removal` value.\n- Spawning onto an occupied cell with `near:true` (or whatever the opt-in is\n  named) succeeds AND reports `displaced {requested, actual, distance, blocker}`.\n  Demonstrated live with the exact reproduction above: a bed onto a bed at\n  [112,108], and a steel stack onto an occupied [100,113].\n- A successful placement on a free cell reports no `displaced` key at all — its\n  presence is the signal, so a reader never compares an empty value.\n- Every other `GenPlace`/`GenSpawn` call site in the mod is listed in the closing\n  comment with its mode and whether it was changed.\n- Zero red errors.","files":null}]}